WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.510
A good lesson begins with a book,
a worthwhile question, and an adult who

2
00:00:04.510 --> 00:00:05.477
knows the learner.

3
00:00:05.477 --> 00:00:06.766
Bede supports that work.

4
00:00:06.766 --> 00:00:09.665
You choose the direction, and
your judgment stays central.

5
00:00:09.665 --> 00:00:14.580
In the homeschooling parent tour, choose a
fictional learner, a book, and a

6
00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:14.958
goal.

7
00:00:14.958 --> 00:00:20.251
Here, a short Aesop fable becomes a
chance to read closely and explain a

8
00:00:20.251 --> 00:00:21.007
character’s choices.

9
00:00:21.007 --> 00:00:23.275
Moms and dads are equally welcome.

10
00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:25.307
Try a representative Socratic question.

11
00:00:25.307 --> 00:00:29.778
Instead of supplying the conclusion, the
example invites a reason supported

12
00:00:29.778 --> 00:00:30.997
by the text.

13
00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:35.468
These responses are scripted illustrations, not
a live conversation or an

14
00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.094
assessment of your child.

15
00:00:37.094 --> 00:00:40.516
Look at a sample narration
and a parent’s review.

16
00:00:40.516 --> 00:00:44.698
Notice what the learner understood, what
needs another question, and what

17
00:00:44.698 --> 00:00:45.839
you would change.

18
00:00:45.839 --> 00:00:50.402
Then close the screen: return to
the book, handwriting, or a practical

19
00:00:50.402 --> 00:00:50.782
conversation.

20
00:00:50.782 --> 00:00:53.442
The classical educator path is different.

21
00:00:53.442 --> 00:00:57.874
The current school pilot supports
teachers using synthetic evidence only.

22
00:00:57.874 --> 00:01:01.864
Review an illustrative record, then
consider the teacher’s observations

23
00:01:01.864 --> 00:01:02.307
separately.

24
00:01:02.307 --> 00:01:04.967
This is not direct student tutoring.

25
00:01:04.967 --> 00:01:07.331
Inspect a proposed instructional next step.

26
00:01:07.331 --> 00:01:10.090
Approve it, edit it, or reject it.

27
00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:12.848
The sample review record
shows your decision.

28
00:01:12.848 --> 00:01:15.607
No lesson is sent to a learner.

29
00:01:15.607 --> 00:01:18.759
The teacher retains responsibility
for what happens next.

30
00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:23.031
Explore either guided path, restart,
or switch whenever you like.

31
00:01:23.031 --> 00:01:26.021
The public demo and
onboarding remain separate.

32
00:01:26.021 --> 00:01:30.292
Bede supports thoughtful work with
books; parents and teachers lead.

33
00:01:30.292 --> 00:01:32.428
All tour examples are fictional.

34
00:01:32.428 --> 00:01:34.563
This overview uses synthetic narration.
